{"title":"Topicwise Test-21 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EE Analog Electronics Part-1","fileName":"078_Topicwise Test-21 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 EE Analog Electronics Part-1.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In the circuit shown,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/8096700fa0d83d437a46928aed9406200820eca6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The transistor is biased at</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 5 mA</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 3.12 mA</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> ∞</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/79e6da8ff42e8662bc68cd1ac3e34be2c5f76bcf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A Silicon transistor with <em>V</em><sub>BE sat</sub> = 0.8, β<em><sub>dc</sub></em> = 100 and <em>V</em><sub><em>CE</em> sat</sub> = 0.2 V is used in the circuit shown below,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b6fdd26b31a14509b5a06ef76e674d5ac0a6d4ac.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The minimum value of <em>R<sub>C</sub></em> for which transistor is in saturation, is _________ .</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 4286 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 4667 Ω</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 5000 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1000 Ω</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/124a27038ca9b532cc4185a1e953cc2e40c3bf42.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":